ups.add(new Task(Id='00TgK00000BTQVTUA5', Description='Service address on this account was NOT confirmed with the customer. It was selected during the 25/08/2026 deduplication by record age only, because no won Opportunity existed on any of the merged records to discriminate between them.\r\n\r\nAddress retained: Penrith\r\nAddresses discarded: Campbelltown / Chatswood / Penrith\r\n\r\nACTION: confirm the service address with the customer at the next booking call, before any technician is dispatched. Update the account, then close this task with the confirmed address in the comments.\r\n\r\nPre-merge detail: deliverables/merge-log.md and evidence/week-02/accounts-pre-merge-reconstructed.csv\r\n\r\n--- Update 29/08/2026 ---\r\nThis task was marked Completed on 29/08/2026. No customer contact was made and no address was changed. That was an administrative closure to clear an overdue date, not a confirmation. Reopened the same day.\r\n\r\nDue date removed. This obligation has no date, it has a trigger: the next customer contact. The 27/08 date was invented when the task was created on 25/08 and is the reason closing it looked attractive.\r\n\r\nThe standing control is now Account.Service_Address_Unconfirmed__c, which is visible on the account at the moment of contact and cannot be cleared by closing a task. Clear that checkbox only when the address has been confirmed with the customer, and record who confirmed it and when in these comments.\r\n\r\n\r\n- Confirmed service address as: 67 Railway Pde, Penrith 2750, Phone: 0411156174\r\nPrompted, not open: the customer did not name the suburb unaided, so the three candidates (Campbelltown 2560 / Chatswood 2067 / Penrith 2750) were read out and the customer chose Penrith 2750. That is the value already held on the record. Recorded as prompted rather than open because a prompted confirmation of the incumbent value is the weakest form this evidence takes, and the difference should be visible to whoever reads this next.\r\nCF-20: customer says the two Patel records are NOT the same household - two separate customers on the same street. Do not merge this pair.\r\n--- Repair 05/09/2026 ---\r\nMechanical correction only. No address was changed and nothing was answered on this task today. The two either/or lines above are still open and are marked [UNANSWERED]; they close when the customer\'s own words are written in. Mojibake from a mangled em dash was normalised to ASCII.\r\n\r\n--- Answers recorded 05/09/2026 ---\r\nSupersedes the Repair note above, which was written earlier today when both either/or lines were still open. The two lines were then briefly filled with BOTH alternatives from a worked example pasted in full, so each asserted its own opposite; they have been rewritten from the confirmed answer rather than patched.\r\nSuburb confirmed: Penrith 2750 - unchanged. The address on the record was correct.\r\nMethod: prompted with the candidate list.\r\nCF-20 outcome: separate households, do not merge. Written to both CF-20 tasks for this pair.'));

